{"id":"chatcmpl-ce047653-171f-4a5c-8525-300a546e8fd8","object":"chat.completion","created":1795245381,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a multi-model consensus strategy for medical image interpretation when the initial expert tool is inconclusive or contradicts other sources. The key insight is to query multiple independent vision-language models with the same targeted anatomical question, then use a verification step to audit conflicts before committing to an answer. Laterality determination required weighing which model provided specific, anatomically-grounded evidence versus vague or null findings.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When an initial expert tool returns a negative or inconclusive finding, escalate by querying multiple independent models with the same anatomically-specific question to build a consensus signal.\",\n    \"When tools conflict on a binary presence/absence question, invoke a verification/audit step that explicitly enumerates the conflicting outputs before finalizing the answer.\",\n    \"Prefer the model output that provides specific anatomical evidence (named landmark + laterality) over outputs that are vague, silent on laterality, or fail to specify location.\",\n    \"Use region-of-interest cropping/zoom on the anatomically relevant area (e.g., posterior costophrenic angle) to ground visual assessment before trusting model verdicts.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Ask every model the same precise anatomical question (landmark + laterality) so outputs are directly comparable; treat vague or laterality-absent answers as low-weight.\",\n    \"Conflicting tool resolution\": \"When tools disagree, run a verify/audit call that lists each tool's claim, then add one more independent model as a tiebreaker weighted by specificity of evidence.\",\n    \"Binary finding with laterality\": \"Separate the two sub-questions (is the finding present? which side?) and require models to answer both explicitly; only accept answers that resolve both.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm at least one tool explicitly names the anatomical landmark (e.g., posterior costophrenic angle) and the laterality before accepting a side-specific answer.\",\n    \"Before finalizing, run a verify/audit step that records each tool's verdict and the reason for choosing one over the others.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":959,"total_tokens":1398,"completion_tokens":439,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":959},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":439}}}